  "notes": "Honesty caveat on the augmented system: the \u0394_\u03bb Wenzl bridge yields a UNIQUE algebraic solution (\u0394_\u03bb = \u0394\u03c1_D uniformly), but uniqueness depends on the b_\u03bc = \u0394\u03c1 \u00b7 z^{n-\u2113(\u03bc)} convention.  Other choices of b_\u03bc correspond to additional physical anchors (e.g. mass shifts of cycle-type-related bound states) that we do not have for the deuteron alone.  The derived \u0394_\u03bb profile should be read as the 'maximum-entropy / y_\u03bb-proportional' prior, not as a measurement.  Option D (LP shadow prices, #603) and Option B (Frobenius co-Casimir, #602) give different priors derived from the LP-dual and the categorical structure respectively; the four options together characterise the \u0394_\u03bb uniqueness class.",
